   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public service law, in relation to certain call centers",
    "basePrintNo": "S6694",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6694-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §65, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6694\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to certain call\ncenters\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to require utilities to file annual affida-\nvits with the Public Service Commission affirming compliance with the\nprovisions of Chapter 330 of the laws of 2010.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill would require every public utility to provide an\naffidavit, annually, thatno call centers, or other facility providing\ncustomer assistance, have been closed without notice and hearing before\nthe Public Service Commissionand that the utility has not relocated such\ncustomer assistance to another area of the State or outside State with-\nout notice and hearing before the commission.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that the effective date shall take\neffect on the thirtieth day after it shall have become a law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would help assure compliance with Chapter 330 of the laws of\n2010 that requires utilities to provide certain call center services to\ncustomers and mandates a hearing before the Public Service Commission in\nthe event a call center or facility providing customer service assist-\nance is proposed to be closed or relocated.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
